        <h2>How it fits into getting your permit</h2>
        <ol class="steps steps-compact">
          <li><span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div><h3>Download the DL-180</h3><p>Print the <a href="{{ links.pennDotDL180 }}" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Non-Commercial Learner's Permit Application (DL-180, PDF)<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a> and fill in your part.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div><h3>Have your physical with us</h3><p>Our provider examines you and completes the medical section of the form.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div><h3>Go to a Driver License Center</h3><p>Take the completed DL-180 to a PennDOT Driver License Center for your eye screening and knowledge test.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="mt-4">PennDOT's full checklist, including the documents it asks for, is on the <a href="{{ links.pennDotLicense }}" rel="noopener" target="_blank">PennDOT "Get a driver's license" page<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.</p>

        <h2>Not for commercial licenses</h2>
        <p>This exam is for a regular (non-commercial) license. Commercial driver (CDL/DOT) medical exams must be done by a certified medical examiner on the federal registry, and we do not offer them.</p>
